1
00:02:26,702 --> 00:02:28,971
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:02:28,996 --> 00:02:30,998
You still love me, don't you, Alys?

3
00:02:31,123 --> 00:02:32,624
I don't love you anymore!

4
00:02:32,922 --> 00:02:34,006
Hi, Silly!

5
00:02:34,523 --> 00:02:35,519
Tripp!

6
00:02:35,544 --> 00:02:37,087
I saw Tripp yesterday.

7
00:02:37,337 --> 00:02:38,379
My god, Alys.

8
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:40,881
He's gotten even more handsome.

9
00:02:40,882 --> 00:02:41,905
Okay, kiss!

10
00:02:42,551 --> 00:02:43,718
I missed you too!

11
00:02:43,719 --> 00:02:45,345
Okay, kiss Auntie Alys, too!

12
00:02:46,096 --> 00:02:47,096
No!

13
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:48,348
We have a problem.

14
00:02:48,432 --> 00:02:49,557
Our wedding planner

15
00:02:49,558 --> 00:02:50,434
cancelled.

16
00:02:50,435 --> 00:02:51,977
Can you please step up for us?

17
00:02:52,227 --> 00:02:53,269
Cristine's gone.

18
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:55,355
It's you and me again, Alys.

19
00:02:55,564 --> 00:02:56,982
Make your groom happy.

20
00:02:57,107 --> 00:02:58,358
You ready?

21
00:03:21,631 --> 00:03:22,924
Good morning, Ms. Alys!

22
00:03:23,342 --> 00:03:24,593
Good morning, Charmaine.

23
00:03:24,718 --> 00:03:25,927
Is Mommy still abroad?

24
00:03:26,011 --> 00:03:27,220
Yes, Ma'am.

25
00:03:33,852 --> 00:03:35,520
God please help me.

26
00:03:35,729 --> 00:03:37,272
Yes, Ma'am? Sorry?

27
00:03:37,522 --> 00:03:39,524
Oh, nothing.
Never mind.

28
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,030
No, thanks.

29
00:03:45,572 --> 00:03:47,324
Is this really necessary, Drake?

30
00:03:48,367 --> 00:03:50,118
Good morning to you, too, Alys.

31
00:03:51,809 --> 00:03:52,851
Come on.

32
00:03:53,128 --> 00:03:54,880
Cristine and I aren't the same size.

33
00:03:56,926 --> 00:03:58,762
Are you calling yourself fat?

34
00:03:59,924 --> 00:04:01,134
Excuse me?!

35
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,811
What did you say?

36
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:06,141
Take that back.

37
00:04:18,021 --> 00:04:19,897
How dare he call me fat?

38
00:04:19,898 --> 00:04:21,232
Where's Ms. Stinson's gown?

39
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:22,401
Here, Ms. Perez.

40
00:04:22,818 --> 00:04:23,443
This one.

41
00:04:23,777 --> 00:04:24,820
We'll see who's fat.

42
00:04:25,195 --> 00:04:27,614
If this really fits me,
you're in trouble!

43
00:04:29,116 --> 00:04:30,157
One...

44
00:04:30,158 --> 00:04:30,951
Two...

45
00:04:30,951 --> 00:04:31,951
Three!

46
00:04:32,744 --> 00:04:34,663
Ms. Alys, the gown might get damaged!

47
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,164
Shut up!

48
00:04:36,456 --> 00:04:37,706
On the count of three,
you're gonna zip it up.

49
00:04:37,707 --> 00:04:40,418
No matter what happens,
even if it gets torn, I don't care!

50
00:04:40,419 --> 00:04:41,699
Yes, Ma'am. Understood.

51
00:04:41,964 --> 00:04:42,712
Okay?!

52
00:04:42,713 --> 00:04:44,256
- Okay, Ma'am!
- One more try.

53
00:04:44,464 --> 00:04:45,507
One...

54
00:04:45,841 --> 00:04:46,841
Two...

55
00:04:46,842 --> 00:04:47,842
Three!

56
00:04:50,243 --> 00:04:51,411
Are we good?

57
00:04:51,436 --> 00:04:52,979
Yes, Ma'am. It fits!

58
00:04:55,267 --> 00:04:56,267
It fits!

59
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:10,615
I really am Dana Ferrer
and Cyriel Perez's daughter.

60
00:05:12,117 --> 00:05:13,784
He called me fat?

61
00:05:13,785 --> 00:05:15,454
Who's fat now?

62
00:05:15,996 --> 00:05:17,664
I'll show you, Drake Palma.

63
00:05:20,542 --> 00:05:24,503
I'm very sorry, Sir.
But you may not see the bride.

64
00:05:24,504 --> 00:05:27,256
Don't you believe the superstition?

65
00:05:27,257 --> 00:05:29,759
The girl in that gown is Alys Perez.

66
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:31,470
If we were getting married,

67
00:05:31,471 --> 00:05:34,222
do you think I'll let anyone stop me?

68
00:05:35,098 --> 00:05:36,599
<i>What marriage?</i>

69
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,851
<i>This guy's got some nerve.</i>

70
00:05:38,351 --> 00:05:39,351
But, Sir...

71
00:05:42,647 --> 00:05:44,316
Excuse me, can you
leave us for a moment?

72
00:05:44,649 --> 00:05:45,649
Yes, Ma'am.

73
00:05:46,193 --> 00:05:47,193
Thank you.

74
00:06:11,301 --> 00:06:12,510
Same...

75
00:06:12,511 --> 00:06:13,178
old...

76
00:06:13,428 --> 00:06:14,428
Alys.

77
00:06:15,931 --> 00:06:16,806
<i>Huh?</i>

78
00:06:16,806 --> 00:06:17,806
<i>That's it?</i>

79
00:06:18,099 --> 00:06:21,435
<i>I could barely breathe
just to fit into Cristine's gown.</i>

80
00:06:21,436 --> 00:06:22,853
<i>And that's all he said?</i>

81
00:06:22,854 --> 00:06:24,356
<i>Same old Alys?</i>

82
00:06:26,274 --> 00:06:27,776
So?

83
00:06:28,693 --> 00:06:30,654
Where's the next destination?

84
00:06:31,363 --> 00:06:32,739
Drake, what are we doing here?

85
00:06:37,536 --> 00:06:38,662
What are we doing, Alys?

86
00:06:39,412 --> 00:06:41,915
<i>Why the hell is
everything so confusing?</i>

87
00:06:42,165 --> 00:06:43,374
<i>Ever since I met Drake,</i>

88
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:45,460
<i>“Complicated” became my middle name.</i>

89
00:06:46,628 --> 00:06:47,671
Fuck off, Drake!

90
00:06:53,635 --> 00:06:54,719
Yes, Drake.

91
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:56,805
This is who I am.

92
00:06:57,931 --> 00:07:00,684
I'm not the same old
Alys that you left years ago.

93
00:07:01,393 --> 00:07:03,019
You left me, remember?

94
00:07:03,144 --> 00:07:05,187
You left me to freakin’ grow up.

95
00:07:05,188 --> 00:07:06,772
Now, I curse.

96
00:07:06,773 --> 00:07:09,317
I drink —
Hell, I even gamble if I want to.

97
00:07:09,901 --> 00:07:11,193
Look at me.

98
00:07:11,194 --> 00:07:12,279
I grew up.

99
00:07:12,696 --> 00:07:15,198
And I don't want to be
with you any longer.

100
00:07:15,448 --> 00:07:17,324
So, please, please...

101
00:07:17,325 --> 00:07:19,119
Leave me alone!

102
00:07:19,286 --> 00:07:20,786
Please don't start where we left off,

103
00:07:20,787 --> 00:07:23,123
because I don't want
to start over with you.

104
00:07:23,957 --> 00:07:26,709
I want to continue
living my life as it is.

105
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:27,961
Peacefully.

106
00:07:28,253 --> 00:07:30,380
I can take whatever
you give me, Alys.

107
00:07:31,464 --> 00:07:34,009
But don't underestimate
how I feel about you.

108
00:07:34,301 --> 00:07:36,052
Childish or not, you're still Alys...

109
00:07:37,304 --> 00:07:38,638
I don't want to be with you!

110
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:41,349
What the hell is
fucking wrong with you?

111
00:07:42,475 --> 00:07:43,976
Are you fucking obsessed with me?

112
00:07:43,977 --> 00:07:45,895
You're getting married to Cristine!

113
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:47,730
Are you insane?!

114
00:07:47,856 --> 00:07:50,108
I still have time to back out, Alys.

115
00:08:24,351 --> 00:08:26,560
Please!

116
00:08:26,561 --> 00:08:29,564
Drake!

117
00:08:31,066 --> 00:08:34,735
Drink and forget.

118
00:08:34,736 --> 00:08:36,571
Drink until you forget.

119
00:08:41,326 --> 00:08:43,161
Can you feel that?

120
00:08:43,828 --> 00:08:47,040
That's the heartbeat of a man
who's obsessed with you.

121
00:08:47,332 --> 00:08:48,667
Throw me a bone, Alys.

122
00:08:48,797 --> 00:08:51,216
I'll pick it up for you,
no matter what.

123
00:08:53,046 --> 00:08:54,339
I'm yours, Alys.

124
00:08:54,918 --> 00:08:56,211
So, deal with it.

125
00:08:57,597 --> 00:08:59,277
<i>All the complications are coming back.</i>

126
00:08:59,302 --> 00:09:01,513
<i>And I really don't quite like it.</i>

127
00:09:02,889 --> 00:09:05,307
<i>Tonight, I'm coming clean.</i>

128
00:09:05,308 --> 00:09:07,593
<i>I don't want to fight with Tripp.</i>

129
00:09:07,618 --> 00:09:09,328
<i>I can't lose him.</i>

130
00:09:09,353 --> 00:09:11,438
<i>Hell, I don't want to lose him.</i>

131
00:09:13,913 --> 00:09:16,373
I gave your heart back
a long time ago, Drake.

132
00:09:16,467 --> 00:09:18,386
Find anyone else but me!

133
00:09:18,905 --> 00:09:20,740
You won't get anything
from me anymore.

134
00:09:20,896 --> 00:09:22,732
I'm happy with you, Alys.

135
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:24,281
So, I'll stay.

136
00:09:28,748 --> 00:09:29,748
You...

137
00:09:30,583 --> 00:09:31,835
disgust me!

138
00:11:47,804 --> 00:11:49,388
Manang, where is Tripp?

139
00:11:49,389 --> 00:11:50,974
In his office, Ma'am.

140
00:12:00,817 --> 00:12:02,568
Hey!

141
00:12:02,569 --> 00:12:04,399
Are we getting married now, Perez?

142
00:12:05,405 --> 00:12:06,947
Ha ha ha.

143
00:12:06,948 --> 00:12:08,908
Very funny.

144
00:12:10,451 --> 00:12:12,079
What's with the wedding gown?

145
00:12:15,542 --> 00:12:16,710
Let me guess.

146
00:12:17,428 --> 00:12:18,516
Runaway Bride?

147
00:12:20,217 --> 00:12:21,218
I told you,

148
00:12:21,837 --> 00:12:23,338
stop watching too many movies?

149
00:12:26,936 --> 00:12:27,936
Tripp...

150
00:12:30,221 --> 00:12:31,221
What's wrong?

151
00:12:35,268 --> 00:12:37,895
Well, I'm wearing a wedding gown.

152
00:12:37,896 --> 00:12:39,594
And you look decent enough.

153
00:12:41,190 --> 00:12:42,923
The only thing missing is the ring.

154
00:12:44,762 --> 00:12:46,638
Are you proposing to me, Perez?

155
00:13:09,719 --> 00:13:11,929
I'll have to speak to Uncle Cyriel first.

156
00:13:11,930 --> 00:13:12,930
Okay?

157
00:13:13,321 --> 00:13:14,333
Slow down.

158
00:13:14,766 --> 00:13:15,794
Wow.

159
00:13:16,059 --> 00:13:17,059
Slow down.

160
00:13:17,705 --> 00:13:19,498
Big words coming from you.

161
00:13:21,749 --> 00:13:23,250
I will propose one day.

162
00:13:23,932 --> 00:13:25,142
Just chill.

163
00:13:26,342 --> 00:13:27,760
We'll get there someday.

164
00:13:28,738 --> 00:13:29,738
Okay?

165
00:13:32,835 --> 00:13:34,629
Why are you wearing a wedding dress?

166
00:13:35,812 --> 00:13:36,979
No reason.

167
00:13:37,004 --> 00:13:38,214
Just a little preview for you.

168
00:13:39,381 --> 00:13:40,757
I look pretty, right?

169
00:13:47,006 --> 00:13:48,103
Fine.

170
00:13:48,716 --> 00:13:49,759
You are pretty.

171
00:13:50,134 --> 00:13:52,408
Wow, that sounded so forced.

172
00:13:53,937 --> 00:13:54,937
It’s not.

173
00:13:56,948 --> 00:13:58,449
You're too beautiful.

174
00:14:00,395 --> 00:14:02,188
More than too much.

175
00:14:11,614 --> 00:14:13,741
<i>Why do I feel so guilty?</i>

176
00:14:15,164 --> 00:14:16,509
<i>This isn't right.</i>

177
00:14:19,789 --> 00:14:21,212
Marco!

178
00:14:22,625 --> 00:14:24,017
You kept this?

179
00:14:24,544 --> 00:14:25,704
Of course.

180
00:14:26,254 --> 00:14:27,254
Cute!

181
00:14:37,532 --> 00:14:38,712
You know,

182
00:14:39,851 --> 00:14:41,400
if Dad sees us like this,

183
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:43,556
he might get the wrong idea.

184
00:14:45,011 --> 00:14:46,262
Yeah, right.

185
00:14:46,287 --> 00:14:48,039
As if, Marco.

186
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:53,072
So, why were you wearing
a wedding dress?

187
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:01,630
You want the truth?

188
00:15:02,743 --> 00:15:03,743
Yes, the truth.

189
00:15:05,313 --> 00:15:07,691
<i>I don't want us to fight, but...</i>

190
00:15:07,879 --> 00:15:10,423
<i>It's better that he hears it from me
than from someone else.</i>

191
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:18,829
Marco, it's...

192
00:15:19,182 --> 00:15:20,204
It's Drake.

193
00:15:37,562 --> 00:15:38,562
And?

194
00:15:39,345 --> 00:15:40,345
What is it?

195
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:46,008
I'm sorry, Marco.

196
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:49,836
Drake is Cristine's groom.

197
00:15:49,861 --> 00:15:53,699
I promise I never intended
to keep it from you, but.

198
00:15:54,112 --> 00:15:56,398
I didn't want us to fight.

199
00:15:58,012 --> 00:15:59,484
Please don't be mad.

200
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:04,414
I'm sorry.

201
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:13,778
I trust you.

202
00:16:15,751 --> 00:16:16,835
You do?

203
00:16:17,398 --> 00:16:18,440
Really?

204
00:16:26,707 --> 00:16:29,418
I trust you so much, Alys.

205
00:16:30,419 --> 00:16:32,156
Even if I don't trust Drake.

206
00:16:38,982 --> 00:16:41,719
So, you and Drake aren't
going to talk anymore?

207
00:16:50,627 --> 00:16:52,921
Two years, Alys.

208
00:16:54,652 --> 00:16:56,404
In those two years,

209
00:16:57,235 --> 00:16:58,945
did I ever make a move?

210
00:17:01,338 --> 00:17:02,359
I didn't, right?

211
00:17:05,055 --> 00:17:06,765
In those two years,

212
00:17:08,559 --> 00:17:09,844
I waited

213
00:17:10,368 --> 00:17:11,786
before I courted you.

214
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:13,891
And now he says

215
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,840
that I took you away?

216
00:17:18,759 --> 00:17:19,759
So, no.

217
00:17:20,930 --> 00:17:22,078
We're not speaking.

218
00:17:24,765 --> 00:17:25,789
Okay.

219
00:17:26,254 --> 00:17:27,625
I understand.

220
00:17:28,327 --> 00:17:29,594
Come on, don't frown.

221
00:17:30,438 --> 00:17:31,647
Smile.

222
00:17:32,316 --> 00:17:35,278
Come on, smile.
Like that, smile with teeth.

223
00:17:35,303 --> 00:17:37,221
Come on, smile with teeth.

224
00:17:44,994 --> 00:17:46,586
I love you, Marco.

225
00:17:47,014 --> 00:17:48,328
I love you, Zy.

226
00:17:53,961 --> 00:17:55,463
<i>It’s happening.</i>

227
00:17:55,916 --> 00:17:58,210
<i>This is exactly what I’m afraid of.</i>

228
00:17:58,382 --> 00:18:00,343
<i>Drake is coming back.</i>

229
00:18:14,763 --> 00:18:16,098
Thank you, nanny.

230
00:18:16,123 --> 00:18:18,834
Please prepare an affogato for later.

231
00:18:18,945 --> 00:18:19,779
Okay po, Ma’am.

232
00:18:19,904 --> 00:18:20,947
Thank you.

233
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:09,269
Marco...

234
00:19:09,704 --> 00:19:10,829
Hmm?

235
00:19:10,830 --> 00:19:11,980
It's hot!

236
00:19:14,083 --> 00:19:16,042
The food you’re cooking, or...

237
00:19:16,669 --> 00:19:18,086
you?

238
00:19:18,087 --> 00:19:19,505
Marco...

239
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:23,259
- What?
- Marco!

240
00:19:24,666 --> 00:19:26,084
I just missed you.

241
00:19:27,781 --> 00:19:30,582
It's only been a few minutes
since we last saw each other.

242
00:19:34,028 --> 00:19:35,316
That's the thing.

243
00:19:38,324 --> 00:19:40,701
You're so stubborn!
Go over there for now!

244
00:19:42,403 --> 00:19:44,480
I’ll stay here, please.

245
00:19:46,265 --> 00:19:49,393
I can't concentrate on cooking like this
if you’ll stay here.

246
00:19:49,418 --> 00:19:51,207
Do you want to eat burnt steak?

247
00:19:54,248 --> 00:19:55,249
Come on, go ahead.

248
00:19:55,274 --> 00:19:57,193
I'll call you when I'm done, okay?

249
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:01,951
There, good boy.

250
00:20:01,976 --> 00:20:04,437
Yes, your Majesty.

251
00:20:05,134 --> 00:20:06,218
Hey, Silly.

252
00:20:47,009 --> 00:20:50,513
This is the invitation to
their annual family reunion.

253
00:20:57,853 --> 00:20:58,938
Oh my gosh!

254
00:20:58,979 --> 00:20:59,647
My god!

255
00:20:59,648 --> 00:21:00,775
What do you have there?

256
00:21:04,610 --> 00:21:05,986
Why are you still hiding it?

257
00:21:06,085 --> 00:21:07,253
I already saw it.

258
00:21:07,775 --> 00:21:11,403
Didn't I tell you that I'd call
you when food is ready?

259
00:21:12,785 --> 00:21:15,161
When the food is ready?

260
00:21:15,162 --> 00:21:16,579
- Marco!
- Is the food ready?

261
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:17,331
Behave yourself!

262
00:21:17,332 --> 00:21:18,498
Are you sure?

263
00:21:18,499 --> 00:21:19,411
Tripp!

264
00:21:19,539 --> 00:21:21,124
- Stop that!
- Why?

265
00:21:21,210 --> 00:21:22,169
I'm not doing anything.

266
00:21:22,170 --> 00:21:23,294
What is it?

267
00:21:23,295 --> 00:21:23,921
Oh!

268
00:21:23,921 --> 00:21:24,921
The food is ready?

269
00:21:25,631 --> 00:21:26,631
Hey!

270
00:21:34,515 --> 00:21:35,766
Will you go with me?

271
00:21:36,607 --> 00:21:37,607
Huh?

272
00:21:38,188 --> 00:21:39,356
I said...

273
00:21:39,773 --> 00:21:41,692
Will you be my date
for the reunion?

274
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,726
I thought you didn't want me to go.

275
00:21:46,091 --> 00:21:47,091
Well,

276
00:21:47,418 --> 00:21:49,545
you've already seen Drake so...

277
00:21:50,033 --> 00:21:52,077
I don't think there's
a reason not to go.

278
00:21:52,738 --> 00:21:55,174
I thought you didn't
want to talk to Drake.

279
00:21:57,079 --> 00:21:58,080
I don't.

280
00:21:59,748 --> 00:22:02,750
But, it's not like I can avoid it.

281
00:22:02,751 --> 00:22:03,751
He's my cousin.

282
00:22:04,253 --> 00:22:05,421
That's true.

283
00:22:08,090 --> 00:22:09,258
So?

284
00:22:10,283 --> 00:22:11,864
What do you mean, so?

285
00:22:12,470 --> 00:22:13,596
Is that a yes?

286
00:22:16,805 --> 00:22:17,830
Bless you.

287
00:22:20,144 --> 00:22:21,479
Take some medicine.

288
00:22:21,749 --> 00:22:23,084
Before it gets worse.

289
00:22:23,647 --> 00:22:25,149
No, I'll be fine.

290
00:22:25,274 --> 00:22:27,318
It's probably all the
pepper on the steak.

291
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:29,360
Hey!

292
00:22:29,987 --> 00:22:32,113
- All the pepper?
- I'm sorry. Excuse me.

293
00:22:32,114 --> 00:22:33,782
You're blaming the pepper now?

294
00:22:34,033 --> 00:22:35,200
Okay, let's go.

295
00:22:35,201 --> 00:22:36,869
Let’s just eat.

296
00:22:37,328 --> 00:22:39,496
Come on, Silly.
Let's get some food.

297
00:22:39,497 --> 00:22:40,956
But I don't want to.

298
00:22:41,332 --> 00:22:42,791
Just eat, will you?

299
00:22:51,258 --> 00:22:52,717
Sick.

300
00:22:52,718 --> 00:22:55,512
Can't come reunion.

301
00:22:55,513 --> 00:22:56,513
Sleep.

302
00:23:32,301 --> 00:23:34,330
No, it's cold.

303
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:37,260
Drake?

304
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:40,586
You're not well, Alys Perez.

305
00:23:42,444 --> 00:23:45,406
Of all the things I hate,
is you looking weak.

306
00:23:46,478 --> 00:23:47,697
Don't you know that?

307
00:23:48,857 --> 00:23:49,984
Of course, you don’t.

308
00:23:50,246 --> 00:23:51,664
Who am I to you, anyway?

309
00:23:55,114 --> 00:23:56,198
Oh, right.

310
00:23:57,624 --> 00:24:01,086
This will be the only chance
I have for you to listen.

311
00:24:02,371 --> 00:24:05,635
Because every time I say something,
you always pick a fight with me.

312
00:24:07,461 --> 00:24:09,533
Why are you being
so stubborn, Alys?

313
00:24:10,667 --> 00:24:13,580
Are you mad at me because
of what happened in New York?

314
00:24:14,932 --> 00:24:16,689
<i>I really want to say yes.</i>

315
00:24:17,099 --> 00:24:19,018
<i>I really want to know why he left.</i>

316
00:24:19,043 --> 00:24:20,794
<i>But there's also this part of me</i>

317
00:24:20,913 --> 00:24:22,414
<i>that doesn't want to know.</i>

318
00:24:23,297 --> 00:24:24,756
<i>Don't listen, Alys.</i>

319
00:24:24,781 --> 00:24:26,031
<i>You're happy now.</i>

320
00:24:26,056 --> 00:24:28,182
<i>Do not listen to a word he says.</i>

321
00:24:28,230 --> 00:24:30,690
<i>He will just ruin everything.</i>

322
00:24:30,691 --> 00:24:32,299
<i>Like what he did to you before.</i>

323
00:24:33,227 --> 00:24:34,869
Do you really want to know?

324
00:24:37,204 --> 00:24:38,518
Ask me, Alys.

325
00:24:41,999 --> 00:24:43,876
I just hope you won't get mad

326
00:24:44,462 --> 00:24:47,721
that I didn't tell you why I left you.

327
00:25:11,974 --> 00:25:14,184
Alys!

328
00:25:17,446 --> 00:25:18,697
What's wrong with you?

329
00:25:22,641 --> 00:25:24,101
I'm so stupid.

330
00:25:25,496 --> 00:25:26,413
Oh, well.

331
00:25:26,414 --> 00:25:27,623
What's done is done.

332
00:25:29,189 --> 00:25:30,208
Here.

333
00:25:30,542 --> 00:25:31,542
Eat.

334
00:25:34,171 --> 00:25:35,214
Porridge?

335
00:25:36,340 --> 00:25:37,548
Don't be picky.

336
00:25:37,549 --> 00:25:39,218
Do I look like I know
how to cook?

337
00:25:40,135 --> 00:25:42,053
Who asked you to do the cooking?

338
00:25:42,054 --> 00:25:44,098
We have the nannies for that.

339
00:25:45,142 --> 00:25:46,309
"Thanks, Dane!"

340
00:25:46,334 --> 00:25:47,335
"Best brother ever."

341
00:25:49,334 --> 00:25:51,545
Thank you, Baby Dane!

342
00:25:51,772 --> 00:25:52,539
Stop!

343
00:25:52,564 --> 00:25:53,564
Quit it.

344
00:25:56,764 --> 00:25:58,181
This little brat.

345
00:25:58,206 --> 00:26:01,334
He acts like he's four years
older than me.

346
00:26:05,869 --> 00:26:07,621
This is pretty sweet though.

347
00:26:13,043 --> 00:26:14,712
Tastes fine.

348
00:26:18,507 --> 00:26:20,175
<i>Ask me, Alys.</i>

349
00:26:20,968 --> 00:26:22,845
I just hope you won't get mad

350
00:26:23,470 --> 00:26:27,266
that I didn't tell you why I left you.

351
00:26:31,295 --> 00:26:32,354
Seriously,

352
00:26:33,147 --> 00:26:35,232
do I really have to ask him?

353
00:26:36,191 --> 00:26:37,229
What's wrong with me?

354
00:26:38,402 --> 00:26:39,987
I'm happy with my life.

355
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:45,283
Do I really have to
complicate things again?

356
00:26:45,284 --> 00:26:46,701
Bestie!

357
00:26:46,702 --> 00:26:48,579
Who are you talking to?

358
00:26:49,663 --> 00:26:50,663
No one.

359
00:26:50,873 --> 00:26:52,124
I'm just talking to myself.

360
00:26:53,294 --> 00:26:54,753
Aunt Dana said you’re sick.

361
00:26:58,672 --> 00:26:59,753
I see.

362
00:26:59,806 --> 00:27:01,391
So, you're staying in?

363
00:27:03,552 --> 00:27:05,262
Great!
Let's do a movie marathon!

364
00:27:11,184 --> 00:27:12,776
I have a better idea!

365
00:27:13,187 --> 00:27:14,772
Tell me everything.

366
00:27:16,523 --> 00:27:17,523
About what?

367
00:27:17,589 --> 00:27:18,673
About Drake!

368
00:27:18,698 --> 00:27:20,032
Come on, come on!

369
00:27:20,811 --> 00:27:22,395
What's with you, Aya?

370
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:24,065
What do you think
my life is with Drake?

371
00:27:24,090 --> 00:27:25,216
A soap opera?

372
00:27:25,329 --> 00:27:27,729
Do I have to update you
on every little thing?

373
00:27:28,862 --> 00:27:30,203
Come on, Bestie.

374
00:27:30,204 --> 00:27:32,339
I was just a little curious.

375
00:27:32,873 --> 00:27:36,001
If they push through with
their wedding next week,

376
00:27:36,835 --> 00:27:38,917
does that mean...

377
00:27:40,005 --> 00:27:41,924
it's really game over for DrAlys?

378
00:27:46,146 --> 00:27:47,689
Ouch!

379
00:27:50,241 --> 00:27:52,785
Aya Pineda, you're such a gossip!

380
00:27:52,810 --> 00:27:54,578
You better fix yourself.

381
00:27:54,603 --> 00:27:57,189
You're getting too old for that.

382
00:27:59,817 --> 00:28:01,360
But seriously, Bestie.

383
00:28:02,027 --> 00:28:04,154
It's endgame if they're getting married.

384
00:28:04,404 --> 00:28:05,364
Hey!

385
00:28:05,365 --> 00:28:06,782
What the are you talking about?!

386
00:28:07,991 --> 00:28:09,701
Get a grip, Aya!

387
00:28:10,035 --> 00:28:11,620
But seriously, Bestie,

388
00:28:11,765 --> 00:28:13,975
DrAlys 'til the end of time!

389
00:28:14,540 --> 00:28:15,790
Really?

390
00:28:15,815 --> 00:28:17,275
I don't believe you.

391
00:28:17,884 --> 00:28:19,009
Didn't you say recently,

392
00:28:19,034 --> 00:28:21,661
"Wow, Tripp's so handsome!"

393
00:28:21,716 --> 00:28:24,219
And now it's "DrAlys forever!"

394
00:28:24,341 --> 00:28:26,269
Seriously, Alys.

395
00:28:27,296 --> 00:28:28,673
What happens now?

396
00:28:29,691 --> 00:28:31,272
What do you mean,
what happens now?

397
00:28:34,257 --> 00:28:35,466
We broke up.

398
00:28:35,491 --> 00:28:36,491
Remember?

399
00:28:38,511 --> 00:28:41,347
Yeah, there has to be a reason.

400
00:28:43,110 --> 00:28:44,152
But...

401
00:28:45,404 --> 00:28:46,737
What's Drake's reason?

402
00:28:46,738 --> 00:28:48,073
Do you know?

403
00:28:51,201 --> 00:28:52,952
I don't know.

404
00:28:52,953 --> 00:28:55,747
And I don't want to know.

405
00:28:57,332 --> 00:28:59,125
Alys!

406
00:28:59,126 --> 00:29:00,586
You should ask him!

407
00:29:02,254 --> 00:29:04,006
I don't want to!

408
00:29:04,756 --> 00:29:05,883
I don't want to!

409
00:29:08,635 --> 00:29:09,970
Listen to me, Alys.

410
00:29:10,888 --> 00:29:12,055
Once and for all,

411
00:29:12,431 --> 00:29:13,807
ask him!

412
00:29:14,099 --> 00:29:16,268
Alys Zyril Ferrer Perez!

413
00:29:16,935 --> 00:29:17,978
Ask him!

414
00:29:18,103 --> 00:29:20,362
And if you still don't
want to be with him,

415
00:29:20,387 --> 00:29:21,763
I'll shut up for life!

416
00:29:22,733 --> 00:29:23,942
Aya!

417
00:29:27,112 --> 00:29:28,572
Tripp is a good man.

418
00:29:28,947 --> 00:29:30,741
Can't I just choose him instead?

419
00:29:31,199 --> 00:29:32,993
Can't I just be with him instead?

420
00:29:34,453 --> 00:29:35,495
Yeah.

421
00:29:36,371 --> 00:29:37,581
You and Tripp,

422
00:29:38,008 --> 00:29:39,268
good together.

423
00:29:40,584 --> 00:29:41,626
But Bestie,

424
00:29:41,627 --> 00:29:42,627
Bestie!

425
00:29:43,132 --> 00:29:44,217
You and Drake,

426
00:29:44,546 --> 00:29:46,673
Epic together!

427
00:29:47,708 --> 00:29:49,542
Bestie, you might have
gotten me sick, too.

428
00:29:49,567 --> 00:29:51,235
- Sorry, bestie.
- And that's the truth!

429
00:29:51,260 --> 00:29:52,302
Sorry, bestie.

430
00:29:58,769 --> 00:30:00,020
Yeah.

431
00:30:01,307 --> 00:30:03,963
We were epic when
we were together.

432
00:30:05,776 --> 00:30:07,018
We had our time.

433
00:30:08,476 --> 00:30:11,521
So, now,

434
00:30:12,616 --> 00:30:14,284
are you going to talk to him?

435
00:30:27,464 --> 00:30:29,966
Fine, yes.
Whatever.

436
00:30:29,967 --> 00:30:31,676
Good answer, Bestie!

437
00:30:31,677 --> 00:30:33,386
Okay, hold on, I'll call him.

438
00:30:33,387 --> 00:30:34,595
Stay there, wait.

439
00:30:34,596 --> 00:30:35,906
- Huh?!
- He’s downstairs.

440
00:30:35,931 --> 00:30:37,014
I’ll just call him.

441
00:30:37,015 --> 00:30:38,809
What do you mean “I'll call him”?

442
00:30:40,370 --> 00:30:41,518
Hey!

443
00:30:41,979 --> 00:30:43,897
Aya!

444
00:30:51,422 --> 00:30:52,823
It's okay, Alys.

445
00:30:52,848 --> 00:30:54,349
Everything will be alright.

446
00:31:09,589 --> 00:31:10,757
Drake?

447
00:31:21,143 --> 00:31:22,310
Talk.

448
00:31:25,188 --> 00:31:27,205
It’s because you made me
your whole world

449
00:31:27,691 --> 00:31:29,455
back then, Alys.

450
00:31:47,794 --> 00:31:48,879
That's it?

451
00:31:53,592 --> 00:31:55,343
No complicated shit?

452
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:01,058
No mind-bending reason?

453
00:32:03,977 --> 00:32:06,480
Not even an implausible excuse?

454
00:32:07,898 --> 00:32:08,898
That’s it?

455
00:32:09,709 --> 00:32:11,126
Just plain...

456
00:32:11,151 --> 00:32:15,072
"I can't keep a love life and keep
living my life at the same time?"

457
00:32:16,656 --> 00:32:18,282
That's crap.

458
00:32:18,283 --> 00:32:19,367
That's it?

459
00:32:20,410 --> 00:32:22,329
It’s not only that, Alys.

460
00:32:25,475 --> 00:32:28,424
I left you because you were
ruining your life over me.

461
00:32:34,028 --> 00:32:37,362
You don't get to decide
what's good for me, Drake!

462
00:32:38,887 --> 00:32:40,347
Back then, I could.

463
00:32:43,196 --> 00:32:45,240
I was your boyfriend, Alys.

464
00:32:48,105 --> 00:32:49,393
And I knew,

465
00:32:50,228 --> 00:32:52,846
that we'd ruin each other
if we stayed that way.

466
00:32:53,360 --> 00:32:56,526
It wasn't worth it when you
had so much ahead of you.

467
00:32:57,239 --> 00:32:58,823
I wasn't pulling shits!

468
00:32:59,324 --> 00:33:00,760
What is this about?

469
00:33:00,856 --> 00:33:02,316
My studies?

470
00:33:03,922 --> 00:33:05,487
News flash.

471
00:33:05,904 --> 00:33:08,363
I was never smart,

472
00:33:08,583 --> 00:33:09,960
Mr. Genius.

473
00:33:10,703 --> 00:33:14,123
You think leaving me would
magically make me smart?

474
00:33:15,298 --> 00:33:16,298
It didn't.

475
00:33:20,303 --> 00:33:21,680
I dropped out.

476
00:33:22,681 --> 00:33:24,057
Did you know that, Drake?

477
00:33:24,891 --> 00:33:27,227
Did you know what
you put me through?

478
00:33:39,114 --> 00:33:40,740
You were my boyfriend!

479
00:33:42,909 --> 00:33:44,494
Weren't you?!

480
00:33:45,495 --> 00:33:47,621
You were supposed to be the one

481
00:33:47,622 --> 00:33:50,292
helping and encouraging me to study!

482
00:33:53,503 --> 00:33:55,060
I was in New York.

483
00:33:56,933 --> 00:33:59,686
I was alone.
I barely knew anyone.

484
00:34:00,594 --> 00:34:02,497
Shit, I’ve never

485
00:34:02,804 --> 00:34:06,099
felt so alone.

486
00:34:07,851 --> 00:34:09,352
Only then, Drake.

487
00:34:10,478 --> 00:34:11,897
Wherever I'd look,

488
00:34:12,230 --> 00:34:14,023
I couldn't recognize anyone.

489
00:34:14,024 --> 00:34:15,734
I couldn't talk to anyone.

490
00:34:16,146 --> 00:34:17,772
Drake, I was so

491
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:19,474
fucking lonely.

492
00:34:22,115 --> 00:34:23,617
Do you remember?

493
00:34:24,910 --> 00:34:27,537
The day I left on that rooftop?

494
00:34:28,747 --> 00:34:30,373
Do you know

495
00:34:30,707 --> 00:34:34,377
how badly I wanted you

496
00:34:37,138 --> 00:34:38,765
to stop me?

497
00:34:41,009 --> 00:34:42,761
"Alys, don't go."

498
00:34:46,014 --> 00:34:48,642
That's all I wanted to hear.

499
00:34:51,937 --> 00:34:53,230
That's all.

500
00:34:54,981 --> 00:34:56,524
Three words.

501
00:34:57,150 --> 00:34:58,902
Ten letters.

502
00:34:59,945 --> 00:35:02,197
But you didn't even give me that.

503
00:35:07,665 --> 00:35:09,542
Did you even know that, Drake?

504
00:35:10,664 --> 00:35:14,173
I loved you so fucking much!

505
00:35:15,961 --> 00:35:19,283
To the point that I begged
my parents to let me stay!

506
00:35:22,175 --> 00:35:23,415
Did you know that?

507
00:35:24,469 --> 00:35:26,012
What do you know about me?

508
00:35:28,390 --> 00:35:29,974
All you ever knew

509
00:35:29,975 --> 00:35:32,309
was Alys Zyril Perez,

510
00:35:32,310 --> 00:35:34,520
who tried so hard

511
00:35:34,521 --> 00:35:36,147
to be your girlfriend.

512
00:35:37,357 --> 00:35:38,984
Now that I've mentioned it,

513
00:35:41,278 --> 00:35:42,487
I feel so cheap.

514
00:35:45,540 --> 00:35:48,413
That's what you must think of me.

515
00:35:49,619 --> 00:35:51,381
A little dog!

516
00:35:52,606 --> 00:35:54,692
I was like a dog!

517
00:35:55,500 --> 00:35:56,835
Following you around.

518
00:35:57,752 --> 00:36:00,297
Shit, I wait for your
fucking command.

519
00:36:04,301 --> 00:36:07,470
Is that why it was easy
to take me for granted?

520
00:36:08,516 --> 00:36:09,772
Because you know what,

521
00:36:11,266 --> 00:36:13,381
whatever you did,

522
00:36:14,978 --> 00:36:17,069
even if you did nothing,

523
00:36:18,857 --> 00:36:20,530
I would be there.

524
00:36:22,110 --> 00:36:24,738
I loved you over and over again, Drake!

525
00:36:25,822 --> 00:36:28,908
I loved you over and over again, Drake!

526
00:36:29,868 --> 00:36:32,620
I loved you over and over again, Drake!

527
00:36:38,084 --> 00:36:39,753
And you fucked me over.

528
00:36:41,588 --> 00:36:43,882
I was so easy to
leave behind, wasn't I?

529
00:36:45,008 --> 00:36:48,425
That was the reason you left me?
What the fucking hell!

530
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:52,980
You’re so funny!

531
00:36:56,500 --> 00:36:57,793
I love you.

532
00:37:01,164 --> 00:37:02,457
<i>There.</i>

533
00:37:03,276 --> 00:37:04,363
<i>There it is.</i>

534
00:37:05,362 --> 00:37:08,363
<i>Every time he's like this,
I lose myself.</i>

535
00:37:10,366 --> 00:37:11,909
<i>But I don't want this anymore.</i>

536
00:37:14,662 --> 00:37:15,830
<i>Please.</i>

537
00:37:15,955 --> 00:37:17,123
<i>Enough.</i>

538
00:37:18,917 --> 00:37:20,168
Are you finished, Alys?

539
00:37:22,420 --> 00:37:23,546
No, Drake.

540
00:37:25,173 --> 00:37:28,542
I'll never be finished with you.
And you'll never hear the end of it.

541
00:37:30,136 --> 00:37:31,221
Good.

542
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:36,846
Because I couldn't care less
about whatever you say, Alys.

543
00:37:37,742 --> 00:37:40,579
As long as you speak to me,
I'll be happy.

544
00:37:59,416 --> 00:38:00,566
Don't cry.

545
00:38:13,763 --> 00:38:14,785
Talk.

546
00:38:16,599 --> 00:38:18,226
I'd rather not, Alys.

547
00:38:18,893 --> 00:38:21,896
Because every time I talk,
you always cry.

548
00:38:23,015 --> 00:38:24,598
When you talk,

549
00:38:24,732 --> 00:38:25,733
I listen.

550
00:38:26,109 --> 00:38:27,339
When I talk,

551
00:38:28,220 --> 00:38:29,221
you cry.

552
00:38:29,904 --> 00:38:30,947
So, I'd rather not.

553
00:38:31,906 --> 00:38:32,949
Fine.

554
00:38:33,144 --> 00:38:34,521
That's how it is, Drake.

555
00:38:37,537 --> 00:38:39,019
Are you mad, too?

556
00:38:41,332 --> 00:38:44,753
Because I am really fucking mad.

557
00:38:47,275 --> 00:38:49,113
Drake, talk.

558
00:38:52,103 --> 00:38:53,363
Stop crying.

559
00:38:53,970 --> 00:38:55,346
Please, Alys.

560
00:39:01,769 --> 00:39:05,273
You don't get to decide
for me now, Drake.

561
00:39:05,678 --> 00:39:07,769
You're not my boyfriend anymore.

562
00:39:09,277 --> 00:39:10,945
I know.

563
00:39:13,257 --> 00:39:15,480
But I love you so much, Alys.

564
00:39:15,609 --> 00:39:16,777
I loved you then,

565
00:39:17,827 --> 00:39:18,995
until now.

566
00:39:20,663 --> 00:39:22,123
You just haven't accepted it.

567
00:39:22,957 --> 00:39:24,917
Or you just don't want to.

568
00:39:28,338 --> 00:39:29,745
Please, Drake.

569
00:39:31,466 --> 00:39:32,456
Please...

570
00:39:34,969 --> 00:39:37,055
Stop saying that you love me.

571
00:39:37,931 --> 00:39:39,160
I love Tripp.

572
00:39:53,566 --> 00:39:55,485
I'm still in love with you, Alys.

573
00:39:57,492 --> 00:39:58,492
Always.

574
00:40:00,036 --> 00:40:01,036
Always.

575
00:40:03,289 --> 00:40:06,042
You always call me selfish.

576
00:40:07,919 --> 00:40:09,921
But, Alys, how was that selfish?

577
00:40:10,375 --> 00:40:12,613
I put your well being first,

578
00:40:12,807 --> 00:40:14,684
before my own feelings.

579
00:40:19,384 --> 00:40:20,816
I did everything I could

580
00:40:21,140 --> 00:40:23,517
to stay in your life.

581
00:40:23,969 --> 00:40:25,863
Even when we were apart,

582
00:40:26,020 --> 00:40:27,730
I tried to follow you.

583
00:40:39,701 --> 00:40:41,472
But the more I watch you,

584
00:40:43,538 --> 00:40:45,675
there’s one thing
I can’t accept.

585
00:40:52,046 --> 00:40:55,769
You're slowly ruining
your life because of me.

586
00:40:58,412 --> 00:41:02,011
I couldn't bear to watch.
Because I love you.

587
00:41:04,475 --> 00:41:05,800
I love you so much.

588
00:41:10,465 --> 00:41:11,800
Alys.

589
00:41:15,278 --> 00:41:19,281
I can love you without
forgetting about myself.

590
00:41:19,282 --> 00:41:20,282
You can't.

591
00:41:22,577 --> 00:41:24,037
I can.

592
00:41:25,872 --> 00:41:26,998
No, Alys.

593
00:41:30,627 --> 00:41:33,755
And every time you
try to choose me,

594
00:41:35,381 --> 00:41:37,925
there’s one thing you always forget.

595
00:41:39,469 --> 00:41:41,804
I can't bear to watch that, Alys.

596
00:41:43,890 --> 00:41:45,141
Fuck you, Drake!

597
00:41:48,561 --> 00:41:50,730
All I did was fucking love you!

598
00:41:52,523 --> 00:41:55,943
I just loved you!
What was so wrong with that?

599
00:41:58,863 --> 00:42:01,032
All I did was love you!

600
00:42:01,908 --> 00:42:04,327
In your eyes,
all you did was love me.

601
00:42:05,578 --> 00:42:06,913
The way I see it,

602
00:42:07,538 --> 00:42:09,666
you're forgetting who you are.

603
00:42:11,084 --> 00:42:12,752
Are you saying,

604
00:42:14,045 --> 00:42:16,004
that I was destroying my life

605
00:42:16,005 --> 00:42:17,965
when I was dating you?

606
00:42:19,342 --> 00:42:20,551
No, Drake.

607
00:42:21,135 --> 00:42:24,013
Get this through your thick head!

608
00:42:27,475 --> 00:42:28,601
You...

609
00:42:31,104 --> 00:42:33,439
You broke me when you
left me in New York!

610
00:42:36,734 --> 00:42:38,736
I didn't break myself.

611
00:42:41,489 --> 00:42:42,489
You did!

612
00:42:42,557 --> 00:42:43,604
No, Alys.

613
00:42:46,089 --> 00:42:48,675
I stopped you
from destroying yourself.

614
00:42:50,873 --> 00:42:52,230
Listen to me, Alys.

615
00:42:54,168 --> 00:42:55,878
I never ever asked

616
00:42:56,897 --> 00:42:59,358
that you love me at
the cost of your life.

617
00:43:03,970 --> 00:43:05,513
I'd never ask you

618
00:43:07,348 --> 00:43:08,808
to choose me.

619
00:43:10,059 --> 00:43:12,103
If someone has to do the chasing,

620
00:43:12,979 --> 00:43:14,105
let it be me.

621
00:43:15,773 --> 00:43:18,526
If someone has to wait,

622
00:43:19,819 --> 00:43:21,028
let it be me.

623
00:43:22,196 --> 00:43:24,615
If someone has to get hurt,

624
00:43:25,742 --> 00:43:26,951
let it be me, Alys.

625
00:43:35,918 --> 00:43:37,128
No, Drake.

626
00:43:37,712 --> 00:43:38,712
That's enough.

627
00:43:40,590 --> 00:43:42,759
Alys, I will wait for you

628
00:43:43,968 --> 00:43:46,304
if you tell me to.

629
00:43:46,804 --> 00:43:49,140
I'm willing to love you, Alys,

630
00:43:50,266 --> 00:43:53,102
while you're living your best life.

631
00:43:54,437 --> 00:43:56,481
I'm willing to be the fool, Alys.

632
00:44:01,652 --> 00:44:03,029
Just say yes.

633
00:44:03,738 --> 00:44:05,470
Please say yes, Alys.

634
00:44:07,267 --> 00:44:08,884
I'm begging you.

635
00:44:11,263 --> 00:44:13,307
I'll be waiting, Alys.

636
00:44:15,833 --> 00:44:17,126
I'll be waiting.

637
00:44:19,295 --> 00:44:21,376
I can handle the pain.

638
00:44:21,401 --> 00:44:24,530
And I can give you all my love.

639
00:44:25,684 --> 00:44:27,186
I'll wait for you, Alys.

640
00:44:29,347 --> 00:44:31,641
Just give me a chance.

641
00:45:31,849 --> 00:45:34,644
<i>It's been three days
since I talked to Drake.</i>

642
00:45:35,110 --> 00:45:36,320
<i>And I haven't slept.</i>

643
00:45:36,606 --> 00:45:38,066
<i>I've been avoiding Tripp, too.</i>

644
00:45:38,301 --> 00:45:40,512
<i>Shit, I feel so guilty.</i>

645
00:45:41,093 --> 00:45:43,178
<i>It feels like I'm playing with them.</i>

646
00:45:43,754 --> 00:45:45,298
<i>I know I shouldn't.</i>

647
00:45:45,393 --> 00:45:46,144
Hey!

648
00:45:46,169 --> 00:45:47,211
What happened to you?

649
00:45:49,138 --> 00:45:50,055
Nothing.

650
00:45:50,080 --> 00:45:52,623
I'm a little stressed about
Drake and Cristine's wedding.

651
00:45:55,933 --> 00:45:57,018
What?

652
00:45:57,411 --> 00:45:58,829
What is it now?

653
00:45:59,350 --> 00:46:00,513
Tell me the truth, Alys.

654
00:46:01,939 --> 00:46:03,274
Do you need a handout?

655
00:46:04,066 --> 00:46:05,902
And what makes you think that?

656
00:46:06,923 --> 00:46:07,924
Well,

657
00:46:09,447 --> 00:46:10,823
it's just a thought. Because...

658
00:46:11,490 --> 00:46:12,482
Think about it.

659
00:46:13,075 --> 00:46:14,659
Why would you choose

660
00:46:14,660 --> 00:46:17,287
to be the wedding planner
for your own ex?

661
00:46:17,288 --> 00:46:18,288
Right?

662
00:46:18,471 --> 00:46:19,471
Of course.

663
00:46:20,247 --> 00:46:22,624
It's the only explanation
I thought of. It’s either...

664
00:46:23,127 --> 00:46:24,795
You're broke,

665
00:46:25,421 --> 00:46:27,048
or a real masochist.

666
00:46:27,465 --> 00:46:29,300
I have my reasons, okay?

667
00:46:30,051 --> 00:46:31,510
It's none of your business.

668
00:46:31,594 --> 00:46:32,720
Whatever you say.

669
00:46:33,429 --> 00:46:34,721
But Alys,

670
00:46:34,722 --> 00:46:36,389
get it together.

671
00:46:36,390 --> 00:46:37,183
You know,

672
00:46:37,184 --> 00:46:38,350
one of these days,

673
00:46:38,351 --> 00:46:41,228
one of those two brain
cells is going to give out.

674
00:46:42,855 --> 00:46:44,065
That's harsh.

675
00:46:45,858 --> 00:46:47,902
Oh, Alys!

676
00:46:48,110 --> 00:46:50,236
Since you're the wedding planner...

677
00:46:50,237 --> 00:46:51,090
Yeah?

678
00:46:51,115 --> 00:46:52,406
Could I

679
00:46:52,431 --> 00:46:53,807
get an invitation?

680
00:46:54,016 --> 00:46:54,642
Why?

681
00:46:54,667 --> 00:46:56,042
You weren't invited?

682
00:46:56,509 --> 00:46:59,344
You know that me and Drake
are basically Tom and Jerry.

683
00:46:59,369 --> 00:46:59,870
Right?

684
00:46:59,940 --> 00:47:00,940
Of course, I wasn't.

685
00:47:01,620 --> 00:47:02,620
Come on!

686
00:47:02,908 --> 00:47:04,660
Squeeze me into the guest list.

687
00:47:06,212 --> 00:47:07,801
Okay, but...

688
00:47:08,587 --> 00:47:09,546
But?

689
00:47:09,571 --> 00:47:12,114
Tell me why Drake
is so mad at you.

690
00:47:14,151 --> 00:47:15,653
In your dreams, Perez.

691
00:47:17,139 --> 00:47:18,139
Okay!

692
00:47:18,140 --> 00:47:19,598
Then no invites for you.

693
00:47:19,623 --> 00:47:21,292
You'll just have to crash it.

694
00:47:21,993 --> 00:47:23,044
Whatever.

695
00:47:23,460 --> 00:47:25,087
But I do have a question.

696
00:47:25,504 --> 00:47:26,213
Hmm?

697
00:47:26,238 --> 00:47:28,615
Is Drake’s wedding real or...

698
00:47:29,250 --> 00:47:30,250
just a scam?

699
00:47:30,994 --> 00:47:32,871
Why would it be a scam?

700
00:47:33,858 --> 00:47:35,193
To tell you honestly,

701
00:47:35,439 --> 00:47:37,273
no one in the family knows

702
00:47:37,328 --> 00:47:39,162
that a wedding is about to happen.

703
00:47:39,187 --> 00:47:39,771
What?!

704
00:47:40,055 --> 00:47:41,895
What? Explain it clearly!

705
00:47:42,590 --> 00:47:43,798
Just relax, okay?

706
00:47:43,823 --> 00:47:44,908
Spit it out!

707
00:47:44,935 --> 00:47:45,978
The thing is...

708
00:47:46,419 --> 00:47:48,169
I asked Mom, Dad

709
00:47:48,194 --> 00:47:49,333
and even grandma.

710
00:47:49,831 --> 00:47:51,666
Nobody's heard of a wedding!

711
00:47:51,861 --> 00:47:53,697
They even thought it was a prank!

712
00:47:55,081 --> 00:47:56,911
And did you know...

713
00:47:58,055 --> 00:47:59,347
Know what?!

714
00:47:59,473 --> 00:48:00,307
Spit it out!

715
00:48:00,308 --> 00:48:01,976
Enough with the suspense already!

716
00:48:02,101 --> 00:48:03,101
So, here's the thing.

717
00:48:04,186 --> 00:48:05,646
When I asked grandma,

718
00:48:06,065 --> 00:48:07,524
all she said was...

719
00:48:07,549 --> 00:48:08,549
“Drake?”

720
00:48:09,040 --> 00:48:12,000
“I don't know anything
about a wedding, dear.”

721
00:48:12,079 --> 00:48:14,415
“All I know is what Steve told me.”

722
00:48:14,478 --> 00:48:18,148
“Drake's just waiting for
his girlfriend who's abroad.”

723
00:48:18,743 --> 00:48:20,036
Don't you get it?

724
00:48:20,328 --> 00:48:22,538
Jeez, thank god Tripp wasn't there!

725
00:48:23,122 --> 00:48:24,582
If he was there? Well...

726
00:48:24,607 --> 00:48:27,318
It'd be World War II in the Palma family.

727
00:48:28,127 --> 00:48:29,544
<i>No, Alys.</i>

728
00:48:29,545 --> 00:48:32,297
<i>You're not the only girl who went abroad.</i>

729
00:48:32,298 --> 00:48:33,923
<i>Don't assume.</i>

730
00:48:33,924 --> 00:48:35,884
<i>But, damn,</i>

731
00:48:35,885 --> 00:48:38,845
<i>stop lying to yourself, Alys.</i>

732
00:48:38,846 --> 00:48:41,497
<i>You're clearly the one Drake
was talking about.</i>

733
00:48:42,725 --> 00:48:44,894
Drake and his crooked world.

734
00:48:45,739 --> 00:48:46,656
You know,

735
00:48:46,681 --> 00:48:50,935
I always thought it was Shaira
those two were fighting over.

736
00:48:51,535 --> 00:48:52,661
Turns out it was just you.

737
00:48:54,425 --> 00:48:57,095
How about sending some
of that beauty, Perez?

738
00:48:57,564 --> 00:48:58,814
I’ll really kill him!

739
00:48:58,839 --> 00:49:00,632
Hey, just relax!

740
00:49:00,657 --> 00:49:01,950
That's expensive!

741
00:49:11,320 --> 00:49:15,324
Charmaine, don't forget
about the 2:00 PM delivery.

742
00:49:17,051 --> 00:49:18,051
Bestie!

743
00:49:18,969 --> 00:49:21,930
- Bestie!
- Bestie!

744
00:49:21,931 --> 00:49:24,491
You know, this is the first time
I've seen you at Mom's boutique.

745
00:49:24,516 --> 00:49:25,893
I thought you’re
a ghost employee.

746
00:49:26,143 --> 00:49:27,143
Whatever.

747
00:49:28,813 --> 00:49:30,314
What are you doing here, anyway?

748
00:49:31,482 --> 00:49:33,483
Well, I'm here to pick up
Ms. Stinson's gown.

749
00:49:33,484 --> 00:49:35,027
I'm taking it to Batangas.

750
00:49:35,514 --> 00:49:37,141
Wedding's in a few days.

751
00:49:37,451 --> 00:49:38,201
My god.

752
00:49:38,226 --> 00:49:40,644
You'll forever be the martyr.

753
00:49:41,124 --> 00:49:42,709
I don't know what to do with you.

754
00:49:42,882 --> 00:49:43,923
Gosh.

755
00:49:43,948 --> 00:49:46,492
Weren't you the one
pushing me and Drake to talk?

756
00:49:46,517 --> 00:49:49,436
And now you're going
on about me being a martyr?

757
00:49:50,138 --> 00:49:51,056
Ms. Alys!

758
00:49:51,081 --> 00:49:53,749
Both the gown and the
mannequin are in your car, Ma'am.

759
00:49:53,774 --> 00:49:55,009
Okay, thank you!

760
00:49:55,482 --> 00:49:56,774
Bestie,

761
00:49:56,799 --> 00:49:58,758
let's get an early lunch, first.

762
00:49:58,759 --> 00:50:00,094
Oh, no. I can't, Bestie.

763
00:50:00,511 --> 00:50:01,428
I'm leaving right now,

764
00:50:01,429 --> 00:50:05,306
because an early lunch
with you will last all evening.

765
00:50:05,307 --> 00:50:06,599
I know you too well.

766
00:50:06,600 --> 00:50:10,019
If I let you gossip,
I'll never be able to leave.

767
00:50:10,020 --> 00:50:11,855
What about early dinner instead?

768
00:50:11,856 --> 00:50:13,816
- Don't you want to hear the tea?
- Oh, late dinner?

769
00:50:14,567 --> 00:50:15,735
I do.

770
00:50:16,777 --> 00:50:17,987
My gosh.

771
00:50:18,404 --> 00:50:20,029
- Why?
- Gosh, so annoying.

772
00:50:20,030 --> 00:50:22,199
Are you going out with Kent?

773
00:50:23,117 --> 00:50:25,410
Are you getting back together with.

774
00:50:25,411 --> 00:50:27,412
"Bee!"

775
00:50:27,413 --> 00:50:28,830
"Bee!"

776
00:50:28,831 --> 00:50:30,748
- "Bee!"
- Bestie, that’s enough.

777
00:50:30,749 --> 00:50:33,293
Just go already. That’s right, go!

778
00:50:33,294 --> 00:50:34,879
"Bee!"

779
00:50:35,129 --> 00:50:36,088
I'll be going now.

780
00:50:36,089 --> 00:50:37,649
- Bye, Bestie! I love you.
- You’re crazy.

781
00:50:37,840 --> 00:50:39,883
"Bee!"

782
00:50:39,884 --> 00:50:42,802
My bestie!

783
00:50:42,803 --> 00:50:44,555
Is she crazy?

784
00:50:58,969 --> 00:51:00,720
I asked Mom, Dad

785
00:51:00,745 --> 00:51:01,970
and even grandma.

786
00:51:02,405 --> 00:51:03,949
Nobody's heard of a wedding!

787
00:51:04,382 --> 00:51:06,425
They even thought it was a prank!

788
00:51:07,411 --> 00:51:09,538
What is that Tofer talking about?

789
00:51:10,657 --> 00:51:13,827
I've invested too much into
this for it to be a fake wedding.

790
00:51:14,936 --> 00:51:16,645
What is this then?

791
00:51:16,670 --> 00:51:18,339
What is it for?

792
00:51:40,277 --> 00:51:41,277
Hi, Silly!

793
00:51:41,302 --> 00:51:42,554
Anything interesting?

794
00:51:46,325 --> 00:51:47,325
Hey!

795
00:51:47,350 --> 00:51:48,977
Are we getting married now, Perez?

796
00:51:49,002 --> 00:51:50,253
What's with the wedding gown?

797
00:51:55,127 --> 00:51:56,845
I'll wait for you, Alys.

798
00:51:57,521 --> 00:52:00,023
Just give me a chance.

799
00:52:12,601 --> 00:52:14,395
You're the worst, Alys.

800
00:52:17,773 --> 00:52:20,526
How could you do this to him?

801
00:52:36,292 --> 00:52:37,278
Tripp.

802
00:52:38,335 --> 00:52:39,378
Zy?

803
00:52:39,586 --> 00:52:41,213
Tripp, I'm so sorry.

804
00:52:42,052 --> 00:52:43,428
I'm so sorry, Tripp.

805
00:52:43,924 --> 00:52:44,924
What?

806
00:52:45,175 --> 00:52:46,218
What do you mean, sorry?

807
00:52:47,636 --> 00:52:49,559
I love you, okay?

808
00:52:50,806 --> 00:52:52,140
What?!

809
00:52:52,141 --> 00:52:53,559
What are you talking about?

810
00:52:54,310 --> 00:52:55,394
What-

811
00:52:59,023 --> 00:53:01,233
I hate to tell it to your face, Tripp.

812
00:53:02,838 --> 00:53:04,527
You don’t deserve this.

813
00:53:16,665 --> 00:53:19,500
My god!
I missed the Philippines!

814
00:53:19,501 --> 00:53:21,044
But I didn't miss you, Drake.

815
00:53:21,045 --> 00:53:22,421
You're still so ugly.

816
00:53:23,088 --> 00:53:24,173
Stupid.

817
00:53:25,215 --> 00:53:26,842
What do you mean, stupid?

818
00:53:27,968 --> 00:53:30,553
And here I was doing you a favor!

819
00:53:30,554 --> 00:53:32,894
You know I hate flying to Canada.

820
00:53:33,025 --> 00:53:34,318
But I did it for you.

821
00:53:35,601 --> 00:53:37,561
Fine, thank you.

822
00:53:38,520 --> 00:53:40,188
Now, you’re thanking me.

823
00:53:40,189 --> 00:53:41,690
You're annoying.

824
00:53:42,008 --> 00:53:43,760
Why did you go to Canada though?

825
00:53:44,321 --> 00:53:46,071
You should have gone
to the other place, then.

826
00:53:46,096 --> 00:53:47,046
Stupid.

827
00:53:47,071 --> 00:53:48,988
Ugh! The nerve!

828
00:53:48,989 --> 00:53:49,656
Ingrate!

829
00:53:49,656 --> 00:53:50,574
Tattletale!

830
00:53:50,574 --> 00:53:51,492
Bastard!

831
00:53:51,492 --> 00:53:52,492
Flirt.

832
00:53:52,649 --> 00:53:53,649
No, I'm not!

833
00:53:53,911 --> 00:53:54,636
Oh!

834
00:53:54,661 --> 00:53:55,628
I almost forgot.

835
00:53:55,662 --> 00:53:57,122
I met someone over there.

836
00:53:57,602 --> 00:53:58,602
Her name's Fier.

837
00:53:58,807 --> 00:54:00,517
She's so pretty!

838
00:54:01,543 --> 00:54:04,630
I invited her to take a vacation
here in the Philippines.

839
00:54:05,381 --> 00:54:09,008
If you want, I'll introduce you
so you'll have another friend.

840
00:54:09,009 --> 00:54:09,802
No.

841
00:54:09,803 --> 00:54:12,221
Just shut up.
That would be so much better.

842
00:54:12,596 --> 00:54:14,014
You're so grumpy.

843
00:54:14,932 --> 00:54:16,015
Oh, wait.

844
00:54:16,016 --> 00:54:17,101
Where's the gown?

845
00:54:23,357 --> 00:54:24,941
Is this really the gown?!

846
00:54:24,942 --> 00:54:27,735
Oh my god! It's so pretty!

847
00:54:27,736 --> 00:54:30,656
You'll drop dead when
you see Alys in this!

848
00:54:31,580 --> 00:54:33,499
She's always beautiful.

849
00:54:33,993 --> 00:54:34,827
Idiot.

850
00:54:34,852 --> 00:54:36,144
You can't pull that off.

851
00:54:37,327 --> 00:54:38,494
But that's good.

852
00:54:38,956 --> 00:54:40,124
Improving.

853
00:54:40,863 --> 00:54:42,167
You're not stoic anymore.

854
00:54:42,751 --> 00:54:43,877
Just a little.

855
00:54:45,421 --> 00:54:47,088
<i>Please, please...</i>

856
00:54:47,089 --> 00:54:48,632
<i>What the hell is happening?</i>

857
00:54:49,064 --> 00:54:51,607
<i>I want to call out and
ask them, but I can't.</i>

858
00:54:51,632 --> 00:54:53,843
<i>I'm afraid of what I'll find out.</i>

859
00:54:54,471 --> 00:54:55,931
<i>All these things...</i>

860
00:54:56,515 --> 00:54:57,515
<i>Damn it!</i>

861
00:54:57,578 --> 00:54:58,996
<i>It all makes sense now.</i>

862
00:54:59,518 --> 00:55:01,186
<i>The gown, the place...</i>

863
00:55:01,520 --> 00:55:04,565
<i>The fact that the Palmas don't
know he's getting married.</i>

864
00:55:04,898 --> 00:55:07,443
<i>How everyone still
thinks I'm his girlfriend.</i>

865
00:55:08,277 --> 00:55:10,904
<i>All the chasing and the screaming.</i>

866
00:55:10,988 --> 00:55:12,699
Drake...

867
00:55:13,115 --> 00:55:15,325
I just wish your plan doesn't backfire.

868
00:55:16,827 --> 00:55:18,162
I mean,

869
00:55:18,620 --> 00:55:19,746
I've done my part,

870
00:55:20,330 --> 00:55:21,457
you did your begging.

871
00:55:22,916 --> 00:55:24,501
Now it's up to Alys.

872
00:55:25,191 --> 00:55:27,254
If she'll say, yes.

873
00:55:27,838 --> 00:55:30,507
And I do hope she'll say yes.

874
00:55:33,719 --> 00:55:36,221
Wait. When's the proposal?

875
00:55:38,724 --> 00:55:40,266
<i>Damn this life.</i>

876
00:55:40,267 --> 00:55:43,186
<i>It's only been a month since I got back.</i>

877
00:55:43,187 --> 00:55:45,606
<i>But I've gone through so much already.</i>

878
00:55:46,231 --> 00:55:48,358
I wish I'd never come back.

879
00:55:51,778 --> 00:55:53,238
The day before the wedding.

880
00:55:55,407 --> 00:55:57,325
Okay, well...

881
00:55:57,326 --> 00:55:58,702
What if she doesn't accept?

882
00:56:06,543 --> 00:56:07,543
She will.

883
00:56:08,253 --> 00:56:09,295
Whoa!

884
00:56:09,296 --> 00:56:11,131
Somebody's got confidence.

885
00:56:11,840 --> 00:56:13,053
Go, Drake.

886
00:56:13,550 --> 00:56:14,760
Shut up.

887
00:56:16,053 --> 00:56:18,597
I know Alys will say yes.

888
00:56:22,184 --> 00:56:23,184
<i>What —.</i>

889
00:56:23,185 --> 00:56:25,312
<i>Think, Alys, think!</i>

890
00:56:46,546 --> 00:56:48,052
Thank you, Nanny.

891
00:57:06,270 --> 00:57:07,279
Oh!

892
00:57:07,854 --> 00:57:10,774
So it's true.
You've been chasing Alys.

893
00:57:14,069 --> 00:57:15,862
What are you planning, Drake?

894
00:57:16,822 --> 00:57:18,991
To hurt my best friend again?

895
00:57:22,494 --> 00:57:24,121
I want us to get back together.

896
00:57:25,518 --> 00:57:26,601
Now?

897
00:57:26,626 --> 00:57:27,794
Why?

898
00:57:28,292 --> 00:57:30,460
After everything,
you suddenly want her again?

899
00:57:32,379 --> 00:57:33,797
You really are something.

900
00:57:34,840 --> 00:57:35,924
What do you think this is?

901
00:57:37,009 --> 00:57:38,635
Highschool all over again?

902
00:57:38,885 --> 00:57:40,178
Nothing's changed, Aya.

903
00:57:44,725 --> 00:57:46,018
I still love her.

904
00:57:46,602 --> 00:57:47,602
No, Drake.

905
00:57:47,941 --> 00:57:50,026
You don't hurt the person you love.

906
00:57:51,023 --> 00:57:53,233
Did you know I almost
put a hex on you?

907
00:57:53,984 --> 00:57:56,278
You hurt Alys!

908
00:57:56,695 --> 00:57:58,405
She barely survived!

909
00:57:59,823 --> 00:58:03,868
I was there!
I saw how hurt Alys was!

910
00:58:03,869 --> 00:58:05,329
My best friend!

911
00:58:06,955 --> 00:58:07,956
Maybe.

912
00:58:08,999 --> 00:58:10,792
But I had no choice.

913
00:58:11,793 --> 00:58:13,770
Are you insane, Drake Palma?

914
00:58:14,129 --> 00:58:15,213
Are you a sadist?!

915
00:58:15,839 --> 00:58:18,050
You say you love her
and then you hurt her?

916
00:58:18,370 --> 00:58:20,956
Aya, you know what
Alys is going through.

917
00:58:21,261 --> 00:58:23,596
She'd fail if I hadn't left her.

918
00:58:23,597 --> 00:58:25,474
I chose to be the villain.

919
00:58:26,141 --> 00:58:27,643
Rather than stop her from succeeding.

920
00:58:28,268 --> 00:58:30,020
She failed NYCU!

921
00:58:30,479 --> 00:58:31,355
She dropped out.

922
00:58:31,356 --> 00:58:32,731
And now she's successful.

923
00:58:32,981 --> 00:58:34,358
But in pain!

924
00:58:34,900 --> 00:58:36,401
Is that what you wanted, Drake?

925
00:58:36,610 --> 00:58:37,610
No.

926
00:58:38,278 --> 00:58:39,237
And you know that.

927
00:58:39,237 --> 00:58:40,237
Whatever!

928
00:58:41,782 --> 00:58:42,865
Stay there.

929
00:58:42,866 --> 00:58:43,700
I'll talk to her.

930
00:58:43,701 --> 00:58:45,077
Aya, do you think...

931
00:58:47,287 --> 00:58:48,664
That's her decision to make.

932
00:58:50,165 --> 00:58:52,250
Only she can know
if she still wants to.

933
00:58:54,586 --> 00:58:56,296
But one thing's for certain...

934
00:58:58,048 --> 00:58:59,882
What you did to her

935
00:58:59,883 --> 00:59:02,635
is something she'll never forget.

936
00:59:02,636 --> 00:59:04,805
Something she'll never forgive.

937
00:59:05,555 --> 00:59:07,870
I can only help so much.

938
00:59:08,600 --> 00:59:10,560
And don't even think of abusing my help.

939
00:59:11,937 --> 00:59:12,937
If you do,

940
00:59:13,105 --> 00:59:15,064
I'll make sure to put a hex on you.

941
00:59:15,065 --> 00:59:16,274
Stay there!

942
00:59:17,275 --> 00:59:18,276
Thank you, Aya.

943
00:59:22,064 --> 00:59:23,064
Drake.

944
00:59:28,698 --> 00:59:30,075
I am watching you.

945
00:59:31,873 --> 00:59:33,500
You reap what you sow.

946
00:59:49,015 --> 00:59:51,226
Dane, how's Bestie?

947
00:59:51,810 --> 00:59:53,395
I think she's better.

948
01:00:06,658 --> 01:00:07,868
Bestie!

949
01:00:08,118 --> 01:00:09,953
Who are you talking to, Bestie?

950
01:00:12,164 --> 01:00:15,709
<i>On the next episode of
Dating Alys Perez.</i>

951
01:00:21,465 --> 01:00:23,675
It hurts too much, Mommy.

952
01:00:23,904 --> 01:00:25,405
Is this about Drake again?

953
01:00:25,430 --> 01:00:27,432
Are you sure Alys is happy with you?

954
01:00:27,804 --> 01:00:29,056
I'm sorry!

955
01:00:29,765 --> 01:00:31,349
Would you like to know

956
01:00:31,808 --> 01:00:33,559
how she looks at me

957
01:00:33,560 --> 01:00:35,312
even when she's mad at me?

958
01:00:35,437 --> 01:00:36,437
Marco?!

959
01:00:36,688 --> 01:00:37,689
Motherfucker!

960
01:00:38,432 --> 01:00:40,112
- You fucking asshole!
- Alys still loves me.

961
01:00:40,499 --> 01:00:41,833
I can feel it, Tripp.

962
01:00:47,407 --> 01:00:48,491
- Alys.
- Alys.

963
01:00:48,492 --> 01:00:50,319
You two!
Just stop already!

964
01:00:50,410 --> 01:00:51,995
Give me a little space to breathe!

965
01:00:52,788 --> 01:00:53,914
Tripp?

966
01:00:54,706 --> 01:00:56,082
What happened to you?

